  "description": "A launcher sits at the left end of a flat 70 m field with distance marks every 10 m. A flagged target zone sits down the field. Set the launch angle and speed, then press Launch: the ball flies along its arc and leaves a trail. Your previous arc stays as a faint dashed line. Readouts give the landing distance, the miss and its side, the flight time, the highest point, launches used and targets hit. Hit targets at 30 m, 45 m and 18 m within 10 launches.",
